    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d516">

                <pb facs="0617" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg609"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">831.24/53a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-07-21T23:00:00-04:00">July 21, 1941—11 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>136. The Department on July 18 handed to the Venezuelan Chargé d’Affaires<anchor
                        n="8" xml:id="d516-f1"/> a draft of basic agreement for the lend-lease
                    program of transferring military matériel to Venezuela. The principal financial
                    provisions are as follows: Venezuela is to receive a total of $20,000,000 of war
                    and navy matériel of which it is expected $5,000,000 of army matériel and
                    $1,000,000 of navy matériel will be transferred during the fiscal year ending
                    June 30, 1942. This delivery date is subject to change if broad defense
                    considerations so require.</p>
                <pb facs="0618" n="610" xml:id="pg610"/>
                <p>With respect to repayment Venezuela is expected to pay $1,500,000 in each fiscal
                    year until 1947, making a total of $9,000,000 to be repaid prior to June 30,
                    1947. In consideration of the broad objectives of the program and of certain
                    very general economic concepts, the entire obligation of Venezuela to the United
                    States would be considered discharged by such payments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
